1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,580
"If AI makes up a number,

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,050
it's my name on the file."

3
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:06,490
My friend told me that.

4
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:08,010
He's an underwriter.

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:09,370
He'd just cancelled our road

6
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:12,010
trip, buried in bank statements.

7
00:00:12,010 --> 00:00:14,090
So I'm building him a tool.

8
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,530
Not with one AI.

9
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:17,050
With a team of them.

10
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:18,890
I call it Bridgie.

11
00:00:18,890 --> 00:00:20,250
Before any code,

12
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,930
Bridgie interviewed me.

13
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:23,690
Seventy-six questions.

14
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,530
Forty-one tasks.

15
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,810
Any AI can build you a

16
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:28,330
demo in an afternoon.

17
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,690
None of them can prove a

18
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,550
single number in it.

19
00:00:31,550 --> 00:00:32,870
So in Bridgie,

20
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,470
the AI doesn't get to say

21
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:35,230
"done".

22
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:36,870
The tests decide.

23
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,510
Then a reviewer from a different

24
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,670
AI company tries to break it.

25
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:42,860
Then a human signs.

26
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:44,380
The statement reader went through

27
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:46,020
sixty-five rounds of review

28
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,220
before it passed.

29
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,420
It caught a fraction of a

30
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:49,900
penny lost to rounding.

31
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,940
A refund counted as income.

32
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,460
A file that crashed instead

33
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:55,540
of naming the bad line.

34
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,060
The kind of bug that ends

35
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,540
up with his name on it.

36
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,580
One week in:

37
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:02,660
nineteen of forty-one done.

38
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,180
Read to the penny.

39
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:05,460
Every figure traced to its

40
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:06,580
transactions.

41
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,720
Nothing leaves the laptop.

42
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,920
Not released yet.

43
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,280
No underwriter has used it

44
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:13,220
on real work yet.

45
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:14,660
Nineteen of forty-one isn't

46
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:15,380
slow.

47
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:18,700
It's what "I'd sign this" costs.

